@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About Clarity Belongs</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Clarity Belongs helps people see what changed, understand what matters, and stop checking the same things manually." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="shell public-shell article-shell">
    <header class="hero compact-hero article-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT CLARITY BELONGS</div>
        <h1>Clarity belongs to everyone.</h1>
        <p class="public-lead">Technology should help people understand what is happening without requiring constant attention.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="article-body">
        <section>
            <h2>What we are building</h2>
            <p>Clarity Belongs is the awareness layer of the Belongs ecosystem. It observes public sources over time, preserves history, compares what changed, and helps people decide what deserves attention.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>What we are not building</h2>
            <p>Clarity is not fear-driven surveillance, a generic dashboard full of noise, or a high-touch managed service. The goal is calm, factual, self-service visibility.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>The ecosystem</h2>
            <div class="ecosystem-grid">
                <a href="https://softwarebelongs.com"><strong>Software Belongs</strong><span>DO — useful software for getting things done.</span></a>
                <div class="ecosystem-current"><strong>Clarity Belongs</strong><span>KNOW — see what changed and what matters.</span></div>
                <div><strong>AutoPilot IT</strong><span>HANDLE — technology handled for businesses.</span></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Our product rules</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Self-service first.</li>
                <li>Keep support burden low.</li>
                <li>Preserve evidence behind alerts.</li>
                <li>Charge when recurring delivery has real cost or recurring value.</li>
                <li>Prefer reusable engines over one-off products.</li>
                <li>Use calm language instead of alarmist language.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </article>
</div>
